[
 "[SETUP — Close Zoom and Teams. In Terminal: cd ~/Documents/cleanmymic. Each page shows a command: start it, read the page, press q in Terminal. Things in brackets are directions, not to be read.]",
 "[TAKE QUIET — Normal seat, quiet room.]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh quiet  ·  press q there when done]\n\nThe birch canoe slid on the smooth planks.\nGlue the sheet to the dark blue background.\nIt's easy to tell the depth of a well.\nThese days a chicken leg is a rare dish.\nRice is often served in round bowls.\nThe juice of lemons makes fine punch.\nThe box was thrown beside the parked truck.\nThe hogs were fed chopped corn and garbage.\nFour hours of steady work faced us.\nA large size in stockings is hard to sell.\nThe boy was there when the sun rose.\nA rod is used to catch pink salmon.\nThe source of the huge river is the clear spring.\nKick the ball straight and follow through.\nHelp the woman get back to her feet.\nA pot of tea helps to pass the evening.\nSmoky fires lack flame and heat.\nThe soft cushion broke the man's fall.\nThe salt breeze came across from the sea.\nThe girl at the booth sold fifty bonds.",
 "[TAKE FAR — Sit or stand 1.5–2 m from the Mac.]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh far  ·  press q there when done]\n\nThe birch canoe slid on the smooth planks.\nGlue the sheet to the dark blue background.\nIt's easy to tell the depth of a well.\nThese days a chicken leg is a rare dish.\nRice is often served in round bowls.\nThe juice of lemons makes fine punch.\nThe box was thrown beside the parked truck.\nThe hogs were fed chopped corn and garbage.\nFour hours of steady work faced us.\nA large size in stockings is hard to sell.\nThe boy was there when the sun rose.\nA rod is used to catch pink salmon.\nThe source of the huge river is the clear spring.\nKick the ball straight and follow through.\nHelp the woman get back to her feet.\nA pot of tea helps to pass the evening.\nSmoky fires lack flame and heat.\nThe soft cushion broke the man's fall.\nThe salt breeze came across from the sea.\nThe girl at the booth sold fifty bonds.",
 "[TAKE NOISE-FAN — Fan or AC running nearby.]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh noise-fan  ·  press q there when done]\n\nThe birch canoe slid on the smooth planks.\nGlue the sheet to the dark blue background.\nIt's easy to tell the depth of a well.\nThese days a chicken leg is a rare dish.\nRice is often served in round bowls.\nThe juice of lemons makes fine punch.\nThe box was thrown beside the parked truck.\nThe hogs were fed chopped corn and garbage.\nFour hours of steady work faced us.\nA large size in stockings is hard to sell.\nThe boy was there when the sun rose.\nA rod is used to catch pink salmon.\nThe source of the huge river is the clear spring.\nKick the ball straight and follow through.\nHelp the woman get back to her feet.\nA pot of tea helps to pass the evening.\nSmoky fires lack flame and heat.\nThe soft cushion broke the man's fall.\nThe salt breeze came across from the sea.\nThe girl at the booth sold fifty bonds.",
 "[TAKE NOISE-TV — TV or music playing at normal volume.]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh noise-tv  ·  press q there when done]\n\nThe birch canoe slid on the smooth planks.\nGlue the sheet to the dark blue background.\nIt's easy to tell the depth of a well.\nThese days a chicken leg is a rare dish.\nRice is often served in round bowls.\nThe juice of lemons makes fine punch.\nThe box was thrown beside the parked truck.\nThe hogs were fed chopped corn and garbage.\nFour hours of steady work faced us.\nA large size in stockings is hard to sell.\nThe boy was there when the sun rose.\nA rod is used to catch pink salmon.\nThe source of the huge river is the clear spring.\nKick the ball straight and follow through.\nHelp the woman get back to her feet.\nA pot of tea helps to pass the evening.\nSmoky fires lack flame and heat.\nThe soft cushion broke the man's fall.\nThe salt breeze came across from the sea.\nThe girl at the booth sold fifty bonds.",
 "[TAKE TYPING — Type on the keyboard while you read.]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh typing  ·  press q there when done]\n\nThe birch canoe slid on the smooth planks.\nGlue the sheet to the dark blue background.\nIt's easy to tell the depth of a well.\nThese days a chicken leg is a rare dish.\nRice is often served in round bowls.\nThe juice of lemons makes fine punch.\nThe box was thrown beside the parked truck.\nThe hogs were fed chopped corn and garbage.\nFour hours of steady work faced us.\nA large size in stockings is hard to sell.\nThe boy was there when the sun rose.\nA rod is used to catch pink salmon.\nThe source of the huge river is the clear spring.\nKick the ball straight and follow through.\nHelp the woman get back to her feet.\nA pot of tea helps to pass the evening.\nSmoky fires lack flame and heat.\nThe soft cushion broke the man's fall.\nThe salt breeze came across from the sea.\nThe girl at the booth sold fifty bonds.",
 "[TAKE ECHO — take the MacBook to an echoey room (kitchen, bathroom).]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh echo-kitchen \"MacBook Pro Microphone\"  ·  press q there when done]\n\nThe birch canoe slid on the smooth planks.\nGlue the sheet to the dark blue background.\nIt's easy to tell the depth of a well.\nThese days a chicken leg is a rare dish.\nRice is often served in round bowls.\nThe juice of lemons makes fine punch.\nThe box was thrown beside the parked truck.\nThe hogs were fed chopped corn and garbage.\nFour hours of steady work faced us.\nA large size in stockings is hard to sell.\nThe boy was there when the sun rose.\nA rod is used to catch pink salmon.\nThe source of the huge river is the clear spring.\nKick the ball straight and follow through.\nHelp the woman get back to her feet.\nA pot of tea helps to pass the evening.\nSmoky fires lack flame and heat.\nThe soft cushion broke the man's fall.\nThe salt breeze came across from the sea.\nThe girl at the booth sold fifty bonds.",
 "[TAKE EXPRESSIVE]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh expressive  ·  press q there when done]\n\n[Laugh for a few seconds.] Okay, that was actually funny. [Sigh, then breathe in and out audibly.] [Whisper:] The birch canoe slid on the smooth planks. [Say loudly:] Kick the ball straight and follow through! [Normal voice:] A pot of tea helps to pass the evening.",
 "[TAKE OTHER LANGUAGE — skip if you only speak English]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh other-language  ·  press q there when done]\n\n[Talk for about 30 seconds in any other language you speak.]",
 "[TAKE NO-SPEECH — the model must not invent words here]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh no-speech  ·  press q there when done]\n\n[Play TV or music for 30 seconds. Stay silent.]",
 "[TAKE LONG — optional]\n[In Terminal: eval/record.sh long  ·  press q there when done]\n\n[Talk naturally for 10+ minutes, e.g. one side of a call. Then you're done — thank you!]"
]